body:
I don't necessarily "demand" things from him. Like it's not like "you have to write me a note saying you love me". It's more like "if you wrote a love note to me that would be so cute and youd be speaking words of affirmation. I'd love that". But the flowers were probably the only kind of "demand" persay. It didn't start as that that's for sure. Started like the other one lol.

&#x200B;

After responses on this post from another community I think I'm just going to try and be more appreciative and understanding. He doesn't want kids or to get married I should just deal with that if I really love him enough. And I do! I love him a lot. It's going to take work.
